let __v_13 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"chilli con carne\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"chilli con carne\",\"chilli con carni\",\"chili con carne\",\"chilli con carne\",\"chili con carne\",\"chilli\",\"chili\"]},\"Chilli con carne is a good everyday meal: lean mince for protein, kidney beans for fibre and tinned tomatoes, and it is the rice, the cheese and the sour cream that add up. Go easy on those three and use five per cent mince, and a big bowl is about 400 calories. The ready-made jars are where the salt is.\"]}],[\"lasagne\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"lasagne\",\"lasagna\",\"lasagnes\"]},\"Lasagne is fine as a meal, and the cheese sauce is the part to watch: a portion is about 450 to 550 calories, and half of that can be the white sauce and the cheese on top. Use less of both, put a big salad or green beans with it, and the same recipe is a normal dinner rather than a heavy one.\"]}],[\"pizza\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"pizza\",\"pizzas\",\"margherita\",\"pepperoni pizza\"]},\"Pizza is bread, cheese and topping, so the thin crust and the vegetable toppings are the good end of it and a stuffed crust with extra cheese is the other end. A whole 12-inch one is 1,000 to 1,200 calories, so half with a salad is a meal, and a takeaway one carries a lot of salt.\"]}],[\"fish and chips\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"fish and chips\",\"fish n chips\",\"chippy\",\"chip shop\"]},\"Fish and chips is fine once a week: the fish is lean protein and the chips are the fat, so a portion is around 900 to 1,000 calories. Have mushy peas or a pickled onion instead of a second handful of chips, and skip the batter on the fish if you want the biggest single saving.\"]}],[\"cottage pie\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cottage pie\",\"shepherds pie\",\"shepherd's pie\",\"shepards pie\"]},\"Cottage pie, or shepherd's pie - the same dish with lamb - is a good meal: lean mince, vegetables and mashed potato, and the butter and cream in the mash is the part that adds up. Mash it with a splash of milk instead, add extra carrot and peas to the mince, and a portion is about 400 calories; with lamb, spoon off the fat before the mash goes on.\"]}],[\"burger\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"burger\",\"burgers\",\"cheeseburger\",\"beefburger\",\"hamburger\"]},\"A burger is as good as what it is made of: a plain beef patty or a grilled chicken fillet is lean protein, and the white bun, the cheese and the chips are the rest. A takeaway burger meal is 1,000 calories and up, so one at home in a wholemeal bun with salad and a smaller pile of oven chips is the same dinner at half of it.\"]}],[\"curry\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"curry\",\"curries\",\"tikka masala\",\"chicken tikka\",\"korma\",\"balti\",\"dopiaza\",\"rogan josh\",\"jalfrezi\"]},\"Curry is a good way to eat vegetables and pulses, and the cream, the ghee and the oil are what make a takeaway one heavy: a tikka masala or a korma is 500 to 700 calories a portion. A tomato-based curry, a dal or a dry-fried one from the same menu is a third to half of that, and the rice is a fistful rather than a plateful.\"]}],[\"pasta bake\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"pasta bake\",\"tuna bake\",\"macaroni cheese\",\"mac and cheese\",\"cauliflower cheese\"]},\"A pasta bake is pasta, sauce and cheese on top, so the cheese and the white sauce are where the calories are: a portion is 500 to 600 calories, more with a thick cheese crust. Wholewheat pasta, a tomato-based sauce, half the cheese and a layer of vegetables in it makes the same dish a lighter one.\"]}],[\"soup\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"soup\",\"soups\",\"broth\",\"minestrone\",\"leek and potato\"]},\"Soup is as good as what went in it: a vegetable or lentil soup with beans or chicken in it is a proper meal, usually 150 to 250 calories a bowl, and a creamy one or a bread-bowl one is several times that. Watch the salt in the tinned and carton ones, which is often the whole day's worth in one bowl.\"]}],[\"roast dinner\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"roast dinner\",\"sunday roast\",\"roast beef\",\"roast lamb\",\"roast potatoes\",\"yorkshire pudding\"]},\"A roast is a good plate when the vegetables are the biggest thing on it: meat, potatoes and two or three veg is a balanced meal, and the roast potatoes, the Yorkshire pudding and the gravy are what push it past 800 calories. Roast the potatoes in a little oil rather than a lake of fat, and put more greens on rather than a second potato.\"]}],[\"cheese on toast\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cheese on toast\",\"toastie\",\"toasted sandwich\",\"cheese toastie\",\"grilled cheese\"]},\"Cheese on toast is fine as a quick lunch: wholegrain bread and a matchbox-sized piece of cheese is about 350 calories with good protein and calcium. The cheese is the salty, fatty part, so grate it rather than slice a thick slab, and a tomato or some Worcestershire sauce on top means less cheese tastes like more.\"]}],[\"kebab\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"kebab\",\"kebabs\",\"doner\",\"shish kebab\",\"chicken shish\"]},\"A kebab is better than its reputation: grilled chicken or shish is lean protein, and the doner meat, the garlic mayo and the bread are what add up. Ask for chilli sauce and salad instead of garlic mayo, eat the meat and salad first, and a large doner in a naan is 1,000 calories and up.\"]}],[\"full english\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"full english\",\"fry up\",\"fry-up\",\"full breakfast\",\"cooked breakfast\",\"bacon and eggs\"]},\"A full English is not a daily breakfast but it is not junk either: eggs, beans, mushrooms and grilled tomato are good, and the sausages, bacon, black pudding and fried bread are the salt and the fat. Grill rather than fry, keep it to two rashers and one sausage, and it is a 600 to 700 calorie breakfast that keeps you going till lunch.\"]}],[\"beans on toast\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"beans on toast\",\"beans on toast\"]},\"Beans on toast is a good cheap meal: the beans give fibre and protein and the toast is the carbohydrate, about 300 calories for a tin on two slices. The sauce is where the sugar and salt are, so a reduced-salt tin and wholegrain bread is the same meal done better, and a bit of cheese grated on top adds protein rather than much fat.\"]}],[\"stir fry\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"stir fry\",\"stir-fry\",\"stirfry\",\"stir fried\",\"wok\"]},\"A stir fry is one of the best everyday dinners: lots of vegetables, lean meat, prawns or tofu, and it is the oil and the noodles that decide the rest. Two teaspoons of oil in a hot wok and a fistful of noodles rather than a packet is 400 calories, and the ready-made sauces carry the sugar and salt.\"]}],[\"sandwich\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sandwich\",\"sandwiches\",\"butty\",\"butties\",\"wrap\",\"wraps\",\"baguette\"]},\"A sandwich is as good as its filling: lean meat, tuna, egg, cheese or hummus with salad and wholemeal bread is a balanced lunch at 350 to 450 calories. The mayonnaise, the thick butter and the big bag of crisps beside it can double that, so mustard or a thin scrape of mayo and a piece of fruit instead is the same lunch.\"]}],[\"risotto\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"risotto\",\"risottos\"]},\"Risotto is rice cooked in stock with a little cheese and butter, so it is a good meal if the vegetables or seafood are the point of it: a mushroom or pea risotto is about 450 calories a bowl. Go easy on the cheese and butter stirred in at the end, which is the part that turns it heavy, and it does not need cream at all.\"]}],[\"paella\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"paella\",\"paellas\"]},\"Paella is rice, saffron, vegetables and seafood or chicken, which is a good combination: a portion is about 450 to 500 calories. The chorizo and the salt are what to watch, and the rice is the biggest thing on the plate, so more prawns and peppers and a smaller spoon of rice makes it lighter without changing the dish.\"]}],[\"sausage and mash\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sausage and mash\",\"bangers and mash\",\"sausages and mash\",\"sausage mash\"]},\"Sausages and mash is comfort food with a real cost: two good sausages are 300 to 400 calories and mostly fat and salt, and the butter and milk in the mash add more. Two sausages, mash with milk only and a big pile of peas or greens is a 550-calorie dinner, and a chicken or veggie sausage is leaner.\"]}],[\"pie\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"steak pie\",\"chicken pie\",\"meat pie\",\"pie and mash\"]},\"The pastry is the part that adds up in a pie: a slice of steak pie is 500 to 600 calories, and a top-only pie with a puff lid is a good deal lighter than one with a base as well. Fill it with lean meat and vegetables, serve it with greens or beans rather than chips, and a pie is a normal dinner.\"]}],[\"fish pie\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"fish pie\",\"fishermans pie\",\"fish pie\"]},\"Fish pie is a good meal: white fish and often prawns for lean protein, milk for the sauce and mashed potato on top, about 400 to 450 calories a portion. The butter and cheese in the mash are the part that adds up, so mash with milk and save the cheese for the top, and serve it with peas or greens rather than more bread.\"]}],[\"falafel\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"falafel\",\"falafels\"]},\"Falafel is chickpeas, herbs and spices, so it brings fibre and protein that a meat burger does not have, and it is fried or baked in oil: four falafel are about 220 calories. Baked falafel or the ones you cook at home in a little oil are lighter than a takeaway wrap, and a salad with them is a proper meal.\"]}],[\"gravy\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"gravy\",\"gravies\",\"onion gravy\",\"bisto\"]},\"Gravy is not the calorie problem on a plate - a ladleful is about 30 to 60 calories - it is the salt, and a stock cube or granules carries most of a day's worth in one jug. Make it from the roasting juices with a spoonful of flour and a little of the vegetable water, and it is the cheapest flavour on the table.\"]}],[\"toad in the hole\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"toad in the hole\",\"sausage and yorkshire\",\"sausages in batter\"]},\"Toad in the hole is sausages baked in Yorkshire pudding batter, so it is sausage, flour, egg and milk with a lot of oil in the tin: a good plateful is 600 to 800 calories. Two sausages each rather than four, a lot of greens or carrots on the side, and onion gravy rather than a jug of it, and it is a decent dinner.\"]}],[\"quiche\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"quiche\",\"flans\",\"savoury tart\",\"savoury flan\"]},\"A quiche is eggs and cream in pastry, so the pastry and the cream are where the calories are: a shop slice is 350 to 450 calories and a lot of salt in the ham and cheese ones. A crustless one baked in a lined tin, or a frittata, gives you the same lunch with about half the calories, and salad on the side is what makes it a meal.\"]}],[\"dhal\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"dhal\",\"dal\",\"daal\",\"lentil curry\",\"tarka dal\",\"chana masala\"]},\"Dhal is lentils simmered with spices, which makes it one of the best cheap dinners there is: about 200 calories a bowl with 12g of protein and plenty of fibre. The ghee or the cream stirred in at the end is the part to watch, and a bowl with rice or a chapati and some spinach is a complete meal.\"]}],[\"hot dog\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"hot dog\",\"hot dogs\",\"hotdog\",\"hotdogs\",\"corn dog\"]},\"A hot dog is a frankfurter in a soft bun: the sausage is processed meat and salty, about 150 calories on its own, and the bun and the sauces take it to 300 to 350. One at a match or a barbecue is fine; the everyday version is a grilled chicken or veggie sausage in a wholemeal bun with onions and mustard rather than ketchup and mayo.\"]}],[\"butty\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"chip butty\",\"chip barm\",\"chip muffin\",\"sausage butty\",\"sausage sandwich\",\"bacon butty\",\"bacon sandwich\"]},\"A butty is bread with something fried in it, so the bread is the carbohydrate and the filling is the fat and the salt: a chip butty is about 450 calories, a bacon or sausage one 350 to 450, and none of them bring any vegetables. It is a good cheap lunch now and then; have it with a piece of fruit or some salad and it stops being the whole meal.\"]}],[\"chow mein\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"chow mein\",\"chowmein\",\"chop suey\",\"singapore noodles\"]},\"Chow mein is noodles, vegetables and a little meat or prawn, stir-fried in oil with a salty sauce: a takeaway portion is 500 to 700 calories and the oil and salt are what make it heavy. Ask for it with extra vegetables and less sauce, or cook it at home with two teaspoons of oil, and it is a balanced fast dinner.\"]}],[\"biryani\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"biryani\",\"biriani\",\"pilau\",\"pilaf\",\"fried rice\"]},\"Biryani is rice, meat or vegetables and spice, cooked with ghee or oil, so a portion is 500 to 700 calories and the rice is most of it. The meat and vegetables are the good part, so ask for extra of those, and a raita rather than a creamy sauce keeps it lighter.\"]}],[\"flapjack\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"flapjack\",\"flapjacks\",\"cereal bar\",\"granola bar\",\"breakfast bar\"]},\"A flapjack is oats held together with butter, syrup and sugar, so it is a biscuit with fibre in it: a shop one is 200 to 250 calories and 15g of sugar, and a cereal bar is often much the same. It is a better snack than a chocolate bar and it is not a healthy one; a handful of nuts or a yoghurt with fruit keeps you going longer for the same calories.\"]}],[\"milkshake\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"milkshake\",\"milk shake\",\"shake from\",\"frappe\",\"smoothie milkshake\"]},\"A milkshake is milk, ice cream and syrup, so a large one is a dessert in a cup: 500 to 700 calories and 60g of sugar in the fast-food ones. Milk with a banana and a spoon of cocoa blended at home is about 200 calories and gives the same thick drink with real protein in it.\"]}],[\"houmous\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"houmous\",\"hummus\",\"humous\",\"houmus\"]},\"Houmous is a good thing to have in the fridge: chickpeas, tahini, lemon and oil, so it brings fibre and a little protein, and two tablespoons is about 100 calories. The oil and tahini are where the calories are and the dippers are what decide the snack, so carrot, cucumber and pepper with it rather than half a bag of pitta.\"]}],[\"coleslaw\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"coleslaw\",\"slaw\"]},\"Coleslaw is cabbage and carrot in a dressing, so the vegetables are the good part and the mayonnaise is the rest: a heaped tablespoon is about 100 calories, most of it oil. A yogurt or half-mayo dressing, or vinegar and a little oil, turns it into a genuinely light side, and it counts as a portion of veg either way.\"]}],[\"pasty\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cornish pasty\",\"pasty\",\"pasty company\",\"steak bake\"]},\"A pasty is pastry, potato and a little meat, and the pastry is the half of it: a large one is 500 to 700 calories and a lot of salt. A small one with a salad or some fruit is a lunch; a large one plus chips is lunch and dinner in one, and the filling is mostly potato rather than meat.\"]}],[\"sausage roll\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sausage roll\",\"sausage rolls\",\"sausage sandwich\",\"sausage butty\"]},\"A sausage roll is sausage meat in puff pastry, so it is fat and salt in a small package: a standard one is about 300 to 350 calories and a big bakery one around 500. Two of them and a coffee is a full lunch for most people, so one with something with fibre - a piece of fruit, some soup - is the better way to have it.\"]}],[\"nuggets\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"chicken nuggets\",\"nuggets\",\"chicken goujons\",\"goujons\",\"chicken dippers\",\"turkey dinosaurs\"]},\"Chicken nuggets are chicken, breadcrumbs and oil, and the breadcrumb and the frying are most of the calories: five shop ones are about 250 calories with around 12g of fat. Oven-baked rather than fried, or a grilled fillet cut into strips and dipped in breadcrumbs baked at home, and they stop being the junk version of a good food.\"]}],[\"burrito\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"burrito\",\"burritos\",\"wrap meal\",\"quesadilla\",\"enchilada\"]},\"A burrito is a big flour tortilla with rice, beans or meat and cheese, so it is a full meal in one hand: 600 to 800 calories, and the rice and cheese are what fill it. Beans instead of double meat, no sour cream, and asking for extra salsa and salad leaves makes the same wrap a lighter lunch.\"]}],[\"croissant\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"croissant\",\"croissants\",\"pain au chocolat\",\"pastry for breakfast\",\"danish pastry\"]},\"A croissant is flour and butter folded into layers, so a plain one is about 250 to 300 calories and mostly fat, and a pain au chocolat about 350 with the sugar. One with coffee is a fine breakfast now and then; two are a meal, and they leave most people hungry again by ten because there is so little protein or fibre in them.\"]}],[\"granola\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"granola\",\"granolas\",\"muesli\",\"fruit and nut granola\"]},\"Granola looks healthier than it is: the oats are good, but the honey or syrup and the oil it is baked with make a 50g serving about 250 calories and often 12g of sugar. Plain muesli or porridge with fruit gives the same oats with a fraction of the sugar, and if you keep the granola, 30g on top of yogurt is the portion.\"]}],[\"ploughmans\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"ploughmans\",\"ploughman's\",\"ploughmans lunch\",\"cheese and pickle sandwich\"]},\"A ploughman's is bread, cheese and pickle with salad, which is a balanced lunch - and the cheese and the bread are the two big pieces, so a matchbox of cheese and two slices is about 500 calories. Ask for more salad and apple and less bread and it is a good pub choice; the pickle and the cheese are where the salt is.\"]}],[\"couscous\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"couscous\",\"cous cous\",\"bulgur wheat\",\"bulghur\"]},\"Couscous is steamed semolina, so it is much like rice or pasta: about 110 calories per 100g cooked, and it is what goes with it and how much of it that decides the meal. It takes flavour from lemon, herbs and roasted vegetables better than rice does, so it is a good base for a salad, and a fistful dry is a portion.\"]}],[\"fish finger sandwich\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"fish finger sandwich\",\"fish finger butty\",\"fish fingers\",\"fish sticks\"]},\"Fish fingers are fish in breadcrumbs: four of them are about 200 calories and the breadcrumbs are fried, so a sandwich of them with butter and ketchup comes to about 500. Grilled rather than fried, wholemeal bread and a little ketchup with no butter is the same lunch at 400, and it is a decent source of protein and omega-3 for the price.\"]}],[\"noodles\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"instant noodles\",\"pot noodle\",\"noodle\",\"noodles\",\"ramen\",\"super noodles\"]},\"Instant noodles are mostly white carbohydrate and salt: a packet is 350 to 400 calories and often half a day's salt in the flavour sachet. Use half the sachet, add an egg, spinach or frozen peas, and it becomes a quick meal rather than a snack, which is the difference between the packet and the pot.\"]}],[\"salad\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"salad\",\"salads\",\"side salad\",\"green salad\",\"caesar salad\"]},\"A salad is as good as the dressing: leaves and vegetables are almost free calorie-wise, and two tablespoons of oily dressing is 150 calories of pure fat. Keep the dressing on the side and use a little, add protein - egg, tuna, chicken, chickpeas, cheese - and a salad is a real meal rather than a side. A bought Caesar or pasta salad is a different thing entirely, often 400 calories or more.\"]}],[\"chips\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"chips\",\"french fries\",\"fries\",\"oven chips\",\"chips from the chippy\"]},\"Chips are potatoes and oil, and oven chips have about a third of the fat of fried ones: a portion of oven chips is 200 to 250 calories against 400 or more for a chippy portion. Leave the skins on, spread them out so they crisp rather than steam, and have them with protein and vegetables rather than as the whole meal.\"]}],[\"takeaway\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"takeaway\",\"take away\",\"takeout\",\"take out\",\"chinese takeaway\",\"indian takeaway\"]},\"A takeaway is not automatically bad, but the portions and the oil are bigger than what you would cook: a Chinese or Indian takeaway for one is usually 900 to 1,200 calories. Order one dish rather than three, with plain rice rather than fried, and eat half and keep the rest for tomorrow.\"]}],[\"halloumi\",{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"halloumi\",\"halloumi fries\",\"veggie burger\",\"vegetarian burger\",\"vegan burger\"]},\"Halloumi is cheese, so it is high in salt and fat: a 100g portion is around 320 calories and a lot of the day's salt. Grill it rather than fry it, have it with salad and vegetables rather than chips, and it is a good way to make a meat-free meal rather than a healthy one on its own.\"]}]]}")?;
